-- title:
--   Coefficient base change intertwines reduced diamond actions on q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $K$ be fields, $j\colon k \to K$ a ring homomorphism, $N \ge 1$ an integer with $N \ne 0$ in $k$, and $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ a subgroup; write $\Gamma_H(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ for the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the matrices of $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose lower-right entry reduces into $H$, and for a field $L$ write $F_L$ for `qExpFunctionFieldC`, the intermediate field of $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$ generated by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_g)$ attached to pairs of weight-$\kappa$ modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(N)$ whose $q$-expansions are realised by integral power series $p_f, p_g$ with $\mathrm{intSeriesC}_L(p_g) \ne 0$. Let $\rho_k\colon \Gamma_0(N) \to \mathrm{Aut}_k(F_k)$ and $\rho_K\colon \Gamma_0(N) \to \mathrm{Aut}_K(F_K)$ be group homomorphisms satisfying `IsDiamondPullbackModL`: for every $\gamma$, every weight $\kappa$ and all forms $f,g,f_1,g_1$ of weight $\kappa$ on $\Gamma_H(N)$ with integral expansions $p_f,p_g,p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$ such that $f_1 = f\mid_\kappa \gamma$ and $g_1 = g\mid_\kappa \gamma$ as functions on $\mathbb{H}$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g) \ne 0$, any element whose Laurent series is $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_{f_1})/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_{g_1})$ is sent by $\rho(\gamma)$ to the element with Laurent series $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g)$. Then for all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ and $x \in F_k$, the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{coeffMap}\, j\colon k(\!(q)\!) \to K(\!(q)\!)$ carries the Laurent series of $\rho_k(\gamma)x$ to the Laurent series of $\rho_K(\gamma)$ applied to the element of $F_K$ given by $\mathrm{coeffMap}\, j\,(x)$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the reduced diamond action with change of the coefficient field at the level of $q$-expansions: any two homomorphisms satisfying the pull-back formula for reduced diamond operators, one over $k$ and one over $K$, are intertwined by the coefficientwise map induced by $j$ (whose image lands in the $q$-expansion function field over $K$). It is used in the analysis of reduced $p$-th-root functions on the modular Jacobian, where the diamond law must be transported from a residue field to the larger coefficient field.
-- source:
